guide-entry-nc-cyberpsychosis = Cyberpsychosis
nc-guide-psychosis-1 = Chrome reduces adaptation reserves; it does not force violence. Medical replacement carries no enhancement burden. Pain, combat, neural failures and overdosing can push an augmented person into overload.
nc-guide-psychosis-2 = Stages: stable, overload, dissociation, acute episode, recovery. Warnings precede escalation. An acute episode is time-limited and is followed by a protected recovery period.
nc-guide-psychosis-3 = Phantom sounds, silhouettes and recognition errors are personal perceptions. Check threats before acting. Weapon reflex warnings give you time to disable enhancements; they never fire a weapon for you.
nc-guide-psychosis-4 = Use the Neural stability self-interaction to disable combat enhancements, choose assistance consent, or reduce visual and audio effects. Nearby helpers can use Help regain orientation: remain close and still for eight seconds. Assistance does not stack.
nc-guide-psychosis-5 = Leave danger and treat injuries first. Neural stabilizer suppresses acute strain, restorative medium supports long-term adaptation, and combined support provides both. Overdosing reduces benefits and adds toxic strain. The medical scanner reports actual condition, unaffected by hallucinations.
nc-guide-psychosis-6 = Removal of chrome raises the humanity ceiling but does not instantly heal adaptation. Rest lowers strain and exhaustion, not permanent costs. Recovery, consent and cooldowns follow the actual brain and survive saving; reconnecting is not treatment.
